Ladybird sizes the positioning area of a local background layer on a
scroll container to its scrollable area. Gecko does the same, in
nsCSSRendering::ComputeImageLayerPositioningArea(), which takes the
scroll container’s scrolled rect for the layer’s background-origin.
WebKit’s BackgroundPainter::paintFillLayerImpl() widens the paint rect
to the scroller’s scrollWidth() and scrollHeight(), and Blink paints
such a background in the scroller’s contents space.
